*> Implementation test of the chat screen and the chat history (client/src/screens/chat.cob,
*> hud.cob CHAT-MESSAGE-ADD; client-surface §4; 05c Chat Message String(max 256)): the line stops
*> at 256 UTF-16 code units (a 4-byte character counts two), the input field shows the end of a
*> line longer than a widget text from a character boundary, Backspace deletes a whole character,
*> Enter on an empty line and Escape close chat without sending, and the history keeps the last
*> 100 messages.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CHAT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-KEY                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CODE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOUR                BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E                   PIC Z(4)9.
 01 WS-MESSAGE             PIC X(64).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE CC-KEY-T TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY

*>   a, e-acute and 254 letters a: 256 code units in 257 bytes.
     MOVE 97 TO WS-CODE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE 233 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE 97 TO WS-CODE
     MOVE 30 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE 32 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM 7 TIMES
         CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test chat a line longer than 255 bytes shows its last 255 bytes from a character "
         & "boundary (the e-acute's second byte is skipped)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-TEXTS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXT
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE ALL "a" TO TL-EXPECTED(1:254)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE 98 TO WS-CODE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test chat at 256 code units a further character is not added" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 257 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE CH-LINE-LENGTH TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE CC-KEY-BACKSPACE TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     MOVE 128512 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test chat at 255 code units a 4-byte character (two code units) is not added" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 256 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE CH-LINE-LENGTH TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE 98 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     MOVE 128512 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "test chat at 254 code units a 4-byte character is added and counted two on the next "
         & "frame (nothing more fits)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 97 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING CH-LINE(256:4) WS-FOUR WS-HEX
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CH-LINE-LENGTH TO WS-E
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) " " WS-HEX(1:8) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "259 f09f9880" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE CC-KEY-ENTER TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "test chat Enter sends the 259-byte, 256-unit line (String length VarInt 83 02)"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT(1:12) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "09830261c3a9" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE CC-KEY-T TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     MOVE CC-KEY-ENTER TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     MOVE CC-KEY-T TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     MOVE 104 TO WS-CODE
     CALL "DO-TYPE-CODE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CODE WS-COUNT
     MOVE CC-KEY-ESCAPE TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "test chat Enter on an empty line and Escape close chat without sending" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO WS-E
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) "|" WS-TEXT(1:8) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO WS-E
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) "|        |" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 105
         MOVE WS-I TO WS-E
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-MESSAGE
         STRING "message " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-MESSAGE
         MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE)) TO WS-LENGTH
         CALL "TEST-SYSTEM-CHAT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-MESSAGE WS-LENGTH
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test chat the history keeps the last 100 messages, oldest first" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CH-COUNT TO WS-E
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) "|" CH-TEXT(1)(1:9) "|" CH-TEXT(100)(1:11) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "100|message 6|message 105" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CHAT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. DO-TYPE-CODE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, code point, count (at most 32): one frame with that many text events of
*> the code point.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 01 WS-EVENTS.
    05 WS-EVENT OCCURS 32 TIMES.
       10 WS-KIND          BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-A             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-B             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-C             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-X             FLOAT-SHORT.
       10 WS-Y             FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-CODE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-CODE L-COUNT.
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > L-COUNT
         MOVE CC-EV-TEXT TO WS-KIND(WS-I)
         MOVE L-CODE TO WS-A(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "TEST-EVENTS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EVENTS L-COUNT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM DO-TYPE-CODE.
 COPY CLTEST.
